    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** serving as the core of the offense, boasting the highest efficiency scores of 72.04 and 71.63, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against Freddy Peralta, and the prospect of facing a slow-to-the-plate pitcher increases his already elite utility in the stolen base category. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** faces a high-upside matchup against Cody Bradford, where a +19% SP skill boost and a +10% park factor drive his projection deep into the strong start territory. **Jackson Merrill** also provides a premium floor (69.72), capitalizing on a rare +13% platoon efficiency gain against Tanner Bibee.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was leaving **Heliot Ramos** on the bench. Despite a score of 44.02, **Heliot Ramos** narrowly missed the final slot, primarily because the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon splits of **Dominic Smith** and the base projection stability of **Kyle Tucker**. While **Heliot Ramos** offers intriguing power, he faces a daunting matchup against Dylan Cease, whose elite arm (2.95 xERA) suppresses the overall efficiency ceiling. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as all operate under \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Risk is elevated today by several arms, specifically the showdown between **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and Logan Henderson, where the sub-3.00 xERA of the opposition creates a tangible threat to our category production. We remain cautious with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** as he continues his recovery on the IL, leaving the team to rely on the depth provided by **Jordan Westburg**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** to navigate the remaining weekend shifts.",
